.TH "tpm2" "1" "" "tpm2\-tools" "General Commands Manual"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
\f[B]tpm2\f[R](1) \- A single small executable that combines the various
tpm2\-tools much like a BusyBox that provides a fairly complete
environment for any small or embedded system.
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\f[B]tpm2\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] [\f[I]ARGUMENTS\f[R]]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\f[B]tpm2\f[R](1) \- To ease installation of tpm2\-tools in initrd or
embedded systems where size\-optimization and limited resources are
important, it is convenient to have a single executable that can
dispatch the various TPM2 functionalities specified by the argument
which is one of the available tool names.
.PP
The options and arguments that follow are either the \f[B]common
options\f[R] or those specific to the \f[B]tool name\f[R].
.PP
It is important to note that individual tools with prefix
\f[B]tpm2_\f[R] can still be invoked, however, they are now soft\-linked
to this \f[B]tpm2\f[R] executable.
And so unlike BusyBox, full functionality of the individual tools is
available in the executable.
For example: \f[B]tpm2_getrandom 8\f[R] can alternatively be specified
as \f[B]tpm2 getrandom 8\f[R].
.SH ARGUMENTS
List of possible tool names.
NOTE: Specify only one of these.
Look at examples.
